---

This project bundles a compiled build of node-unrar-js (MIT License,
Copyright (c) Yu Jianrong), which itself wraps the official UnRAR source
released by RARLAB (copyright Alexander/Eugene Roshal). The UnRAR source is
freeware and may be used in any software to handle RAR archives without
limitation, provided it is not used to re-create the proprietary RAR
compression algorithm — this project only decompresses, it does not create
RAR archives. See https://github.com/YuJianrong/node-unrar-js and the
original UnRAR license text (bundled with the unrar source distribution) for
full terms.
